Release 3.1.1.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 23:24:22

Release 3.1.0.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 21:48:01

Release 3.0.0.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 21:19:45

Breaking. A game quits with View, LB and RB held together for two seconds, no longer View and Menu (owner,
30-10-2026): View and Menu are Windows' and Steam's guide button (Windows' "Use View + Menu as Guide button in
apps", Steam Input's Select + Start), so holding them opened the Xbox overlay or Steam's over the game, which took
the focus and left the game's own quit question unreachable. The play mode closes the emulator on the new chord
(core's play.py); the line at the bottom of Your games, the help and the wiki say so.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 19:43:48

Release 2.1.0.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 17:55:08

Added. The battery is last in the status line at the top, at the right, and says Plugged in on the charger (owner,
30-10-2026; core's power.text()).

Changelog: 30-10-2026 17:18:10

Fixed. Steam started by the app signs in, in Desktop and in Xbox mode (core's outside_bundle(), owner, 30-10-2026): it
inherited the controller reader's SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy, so Steam made its login window without a window and stayed
Logged Off. X Play, the restart after Update Steam and a game started without Steam no longer get those variables.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 16:11:24

Release 2.0.0.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 14:53:45

Breaking. A game's Steam shortcut starts the app's play mode (owner, 30-10-2026: "Hold View + Menu, everywhere"):
Xenia-Manager.exe --play --fullscreen=true "<game>", which starts Xenia in its folder and ends with it, so its Steam
number and artwork names change. A shortcut made before, which starts xenia_canary.exe itself, is still the game's: it
shows (Update Steam), and Y Update Steam writes it again (shortcuts.outdated()).

Changelog: 30-10-2026 14:53:45

Added. Hold View and Menu together for two seconds to quit a game (core's play mode): Xenia closes as its window
would, from Steam's library, X Play or without Steam, where Xenia had no way of its own and only Steam's Exit game
ended it. The line at the bottom says so when a game starts ("In the game, hold View and Menu together to quit."), and
Your games' information and the wiki chapter.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 13:35:58

Breaking. The Open Steam row above the games in Your games is gone (owner, 30-10-2026): Steam's library opens
from the portal, RT Steam.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 13:35:58

Added. On a device without Steam (not installed, or never started), X Play starts the game in Xenia itself, full
screen, with the command its Steam shortcut has (shortcuts.command(), core's platform.start_program() outside the
app's bundle; owner, 30-10-2026: a fallback, as a game cannot be played without Steam otherwise). Without Xenia
installed it says to install it first. With Steam installed X plays through Steam as before.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 12:54:34

Fixed. Steam started by the app signs in (core, owner, 30-10-2026): X Play and the restart after Steam's shortcuts
changed started steam.exe by the lower-case name in Steam's registry key, and a Steam started so never signed in, its
login window off the screen; it is started by its name as on the disk now, outside the app's bundle. The information
popup's text box is as high as its text, up to 0.7 of the window: a text with "[X360] <title>" in it was measured as
HTML and kept four lines high.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 01:30:27

Release 1.0.1.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 23:14:12

Fixed. Update Steam starts Steam again signed in (core's with_steam_closed(): a plain steam.exe on Windows; owner,
29-10-2026): the steam.exe -silent it started never signed in, so a game's Play and Open Steam did nothing until
Steam was started by hand. The status line says Steam was started again, signed in.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 21:56:05

Release 1.0.0.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 21:43:25

Added. X Play on Your games starts the game the focus is on through Steam, by its shortcut's appid
(steam://rungameid/), Steam first when it is not open (owner, 29-10-2026: a game started from the manager); a game
not in Steam yet says how to put it there. An Open Steam row above the games opens Steam's library in Big Picture
mode. The folder browser opens in the game folder added last, while it is there (owner, 29-10-2026: the folder
remembered after it was chosen).

Fixed. The Log pane's newest lines ran off the pane's top (owner, 29-10-2026): they are a view of their own now, the
newest line in sight. A long information text scrolls (core's popup), and the popup closes with B Close in its legend
instead of a big button.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 20:26:55

Release 0.1.0.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 20:20:27

Added. The BC250 suite's Xenia Manager on the portable window (owner, 29-10-2026: the gaming category, after Vita3K
Manager), laid out as RPCS3 Manager: four cards, Xenia, Your games, Settings and Log, the actions with a controller
button in the row at the bottom. A Install downloads Xenia Canary build e6cd2e4 for Windows, the build the BC250
suite's app pins (xenia_canary_windows.7z from its release, 3.7 MB: xenia_canary.exe and its LICENSE), checks it
against the pinned SHA-256 and unpacks it with Windows' own tar (a .7z, as RPCS3 Manager's) into
%LOCALAPPDATA%\windows-portable-suite\windows-portable-xenia\emulator\, where Xenia keeps its settings, your games'
content, the saves and its log beside its program (portable by itself on Windows); X Remove Xenia, with a second
press, deletes only its program; Y Update when another build is there. The Xenia pane says when Microsoft's Visual C++
runtime is missing (xenia_canary.exe imports vcruntime140, vcruntime140_1, msvcp140 and msvcp140_atomic_wait) and when
a newer Xenia Canary build is out (asked of GitHub when the window opens, the BC250 app's notice; the build is never
installed). Your games: disc images, unpacked discs, .zar archives and Games on Demand and Arcade packages in the
chosen folders, read as the BC250 app reads them; played from Steam, never from the app (owner, 29-10-2026), as
xenia_canary.exe --fullscreen=true "<game>"; A Steam mark and Y Update Steam put them in Steam as "[X360] <title>"
(Xenia installed first), with pictures drawn from the app's icon, or all four from SteamGridDB with the suite's key
(RB Steam artwork); LB Folders, with the folder browser for the controller. Settings in four tabs (Picture, Speed,
Sound, Console: 13 of xenia-canary.config.toml's settings, which the BC250 app leaves to Xenia's own window), never
written while Xenia runs. Log: Xenia's folder and the app's log, read in the app. Not carried over from the BC250
window: Play on the desktop and Xenia's own window.
